                <pb facs="0775" n="693" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg693"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 853.00/198.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister of Portugal to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Portugal</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-06-20"><hi rendition="#italic">June 20,
                        1911</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that the
                    National Constituent Assembly met yesterday at Lisbon and adopted the republican
                    form of government for Portugal.</p>
                <p>In making this communication to your excellency, I am directed to assure the
                    Government and people of the United States of America of the cordial friendship
                    and good-will of the Government and people of Portugal and to express their
                    earnest hope that the new order of things may prove a factor in drawing the two
                    countries together in closer association, to the lasting benefit of their mutual
                    interests.</p>
                <p>I avail, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alte.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
